  "notes": {
    "c0001.md": "# Della Frame, Willow Row Mercantile\n\nBiggest wholesale volume, worst payer. Two invoices of history:\n\n- INV-4044, 2460, took 126 days on net 60 terms.\n- INV-4102, 3120, currently 36 days past due, two reminders sent.\n\nWhat that means in cash: every Willow Row order is a four month loan at zero\npercent, funded out of wax money.\n\nRules going forward:\n\n- No new run goes on the table for her while an invoice is past due.\n- Opening order on the next range is fifty percent up front.\n- She replies to a phone call. She does not reply to email.\n",
    "p0001.md": "# Autumn run, 240 units\n\nThe run that proved the pricing is wrong.\n\n- Revenue 5360 across two stockists.\n- Materials, packaging and freight 3715.\n- 33 hours of her own time, costed at 32, is 1056.\n- Left over: 589. That is eleven percent on a target of forty five.\n\nThe wholesale price was set at half of retail. Retail was set in year one by\nlooking at a shelf. Nothing in either number covers pouring, wicking, labeling\nor packing.\n\nBefore the holiday quote goes to Hearth Collective, rebuild the price from the\nbottom: materials, then labour at 32, then packing, then freight, then margin.\nIf six doors will not carry that number, six doors is not the deal.\n"
  }
